  "label": "Misogynous Stereotype: 'Women Belong in the Kitchen'",
  "description": "This stereotype implies that women are confined to domestic roles and are not seen as equal participants in decision-making or perspective-sharing. It is a common trope in misogynistic humor and is used here to imply that the man is dismissing the woman's viewpoint by focusing on domestic tasks, while the child (symbolizing the woman) looks out the window, metaphorically ignoring her perspective.",
